\trowd \trgaph108\trleft-108\trbrdrh\brdrs\brdrw10 \trftsWidth1\trautofit1\trpaddl108\trpaddr108\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10 \cltxlrtb\clftsWidth1 \cellx1596\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10 \cltxlrtb\clftsWidth1 \cellx5993
\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10 \cltxlrtb\clftsWidth1 \cellx10188\row }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 Elves average 5 feet tall a
nd typically weigh just over 100 pounds. They live on fruits and grains, though they occasionally hunt for fresh meat. Elves prefer colorful clothes, usually with a green-and-gray cloak that blends well with the colors of the forest.
\par Elves speak Elven, and most also know Common and Sylvan.
\par Most elves encountered outside their homes are warriors; the information presented here is for one of 1st level.
\par }{COMBAT
\par }{\fs20 Elves are cautious warriors and take time to analyze their opponents and the location of the fight if
 at all possible, maximizing their advantage by using ambushes, snipers, and camouflage. They prefer to fire from cover and retreat before they are found, repeating this maneuver until all of their enemies are dead.
\par They prefer longbows, shortbows, rapiers, and longswords. In melee, elves are graceful and deadly, using complex maneuvers that are beautiful to observe. Their wizards often use }{\i\fs20 sleep }{\fs20 spells during combat because these won\rquote 
t affect other elves.
\par }{\b\fs20 Elf Traits (Ex):}{\fs20  Elves possess the following racial traits.
\par }\pard\plain \s19\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs19\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 \emdash  +2 Dexterity, \endash 2 Constitution.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 \emdash Medium size.
\par \emdash An elf \rquote s base land speed is 30 feet.
\par \emdash Immunity to }{\i\fs20 sleep }{\fs20 spells and effects, and a +2 racial saving throw bonus against enchantment spells or effects.
\par (Not reflected in the saving throw modifiers given here.)
\par \emdash Low-light vision.
\par \emdash Weapon Proficiency: Elves are automatically proficient with the longsword, rapier, longbow, composite longbow, shortbow, and composite shortbow.
\par \emdash  +2 racial bonus on Listen, Search, and Spot checks. An elf who merely passes within 5 feet of a secret or concealed door is entitled to a Search check to notice it as if she were actively looking for it.
\par \emdash Automatic Languages: Common, Elven. Bonus Languages: Draconic, Gnoll, Gnome, Goblin, Orc, Sylvan.
\par \emdash Favored Class: Wizard.
\par The elf warrior presented here had the following ability scores before racial adjustments: Str 13, Dex 11, Con 12, Int 10, Wis 9, Cha 8.
\par }{SUBRACES
\par }{\fs20 The above information describes the high elf, the most common variety. There are five other major subraces of elf, in addition to half-elves, who share enough elven characteristics to be included here.
\par }\pard\plain \s1\ql \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\fs21\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs22 
\par Half-Elf
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 Half-elves are not truly an elf subrace, but they are often mistaken for elves. Ha
lf-elves usually inherit a good blend of their parents\rquote  physical characteristics.
\par }{\b\fs20 Half-Elf Traits (Ex): }{\fs20 Half-elves possess the following racial traits.
\par \emdash Medium size.
\par \emdash A half-elf \rquote s base land speed is 30 feet.
\par \emdash Immunity to }{\i\fs20 sleep }{\fs20 spells and similar magical effects, and a +2 racial bonus on saving throws against enchantment spells or effects.
\par \emdash Low-light vision.
\par \emdash  +1 racial bonus on Listen, Search, and Spot checks. A half-elf does not have the elf \rquote s ability to notice secret doors simply by passing near them.
\par \emdash  +2 racial bonus on Diplomacy and Gather Information checks: Half-elves get along naturally with all people. This bonus may not apply in situations or settings where half-elves are viewed with distrust.
\par \emdash Elven Blood: For all eff
ects related to race, a half-elf is considered an elf. Half-elves, for example, are just as vulnerable to special effects that affect elves as their elf ancestors are, and they can use magic items that are only usable by elves.
\par \emdash Automatic Languages: Common, Elven. Bonus Languages: Any (other than secret languages, such as Druidic).
\par \emdash Favored Class: Any. When determining whether a multiclass half-elf takes an experience point penalty for multiclassing, her highest-level class does not count.
\par }\pard\plain \s1\ql \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\fs21\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs22 
\par Aquatic Elf
\par }\pard\plain \s20\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs19\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 Also called sea elves, these creatures are waterbreathing cousins to land-dwelling elves.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 Aquatic elves fight underwater with tridents, spears, and nets.
\par }{\b\fs20 Aquatic Elf Traits (Ex):}{\fs20  These traits are in addition to the high elf traits, except where noted.
\par \emdash  +2 Dexterity, \endash 2 Intelligence. These adjustments replace the high elf \rquote s ability score adjustments.
\par \emdash An aquatic elf has the aquatic subtype.
\par \emdash An aquatic elf has a swim speed of 40 feet.
\par \emdash Gills: Aquatic elves can survive out of the water for 1 hour per point of Constitution (after that, refer to the suffocation rules).
\par \emdash Superior Low-Light Vision: Aquatic elves can see four times as far as a human in starlight, moonlight, torchlight, and similar conditions of low illumination. This trait replaces the high elf \rquote s low-light vision.
\par \emdash Favored Class: Fighter. This trait replaces the high elf \rquote s favored class.
\par }\pard\plain \s1\ql \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\fs21\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs22 
\par Drow
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 Also known as dark elves, drow are a depraved and evil subterranean offshoot.
\par White is the most common hair color among drow, but almost any pale shade is possible. Drow tend to be smaller and thinner than other sorts of elves, and their eyes are often a vivid red. 
\par Drow usually coat their arrows with a potent venom.
\par }{\b\fs20 Poison (Ex):}{\fs20  An opponent hit by a drow\rquote 
s poisoned weapon must succeed on a DC 13 Fortitude save or fall unconscious. After 1 minute, the subject must succeed on another DC 13 Fortitude save or remain unconscious for 2d4 hours. A typical drow carries 1d4\endash 1 doses of drow k
nockout poison. Drow typically coat arrows and crossbow bolts with this poison, but it can also be applied to a melee weapon. Note that drow have no special ability to apply poison without risking being poisoned themselves. Since this poison is not a magi
cal effect, drow and other elves are susceptible to it.
\par }{\b\fs20 Drow Traits (Ex):}{\fs20  These traits are in addition to the high elf traits, except where noted.
\par \emdash  +2 Intelligence, +2 Charisma.
\par \emdash Darkvision out to 120 feet. This trait replaces the high elf \rquote s low-light vision.
\par \emdash Spell resistance equal to 11 + class levels.
\par \emdash  +2 racial bonus on Will saves against spells and spell-like abilities.
\par \emdash Spell-Like Abilities: Drow can use the following spell-like abilities once per day: }{\i\fs20 dancing lights, darkness, faerie fire. }{\fs20 Caster level equals the drow\rquote s class levels.
\par \emdash Weapon Proficiency: A drow is automatically proficient with the hand crossbow, the rapier, and the short sword. This trait replaces the high elf \rquote s weapon proficiency.
\par \emdash Automatic Languages: Common, Elven, Undercommon. Bonus Languages: Abyssal, Aquan, Draconic, Drow }{\fs20\cf0 Sign Language, Gnome, Goblin. This trait replaces the high elf \rquote s automatic and bonus languages.
\par }{\fs20 \emdash Light Blindness: Abrupt exposure to bright light (such as sunlight or a }{\i\fs20 daylight }{\fs20 spell) blinds drow for 1 round. On subsequent rounds, they are dazzled as long as they remain in the affected area.
\par \emdash Favored Class: Wizard (male) or cleric (female). This trait replaces the high elf \rquote s favored class.
\par }\pard\plain \s20\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs19\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 \emdash Level adjustment +2.
\par }
}
